                            20.0,
                            "i"
                        ],
                        "http://open-music-kontrollers.ch/lv2/notes#text": [
                            "Many reverbs/delays/IR's, when following NAM, will create a horible burst of noise when the pedalboard is first loaded.\n\nThe cause is NaN (not a number) output from NAM.  A reverb/delay with feedback can recycle this bad output creating a nasty digital cacophony.\n\nA few reverbs seem to be NaN-safe including: DISTRHO DIE Reverb, and the X42 ",
                            "s"
                        ]
                    },
